# **************************  Reflection  ***************************

 The pipeline did not run cleanly on the first try because I initially forgot to import the flow decorator 
 from Prefect, which caused a NameError; I fixed it by changing the import to from prefect import task, flow. 
 After that fix, the pipeline ran successfully and extracted 365 daily weather records, loaded all 365 records 
 into weather_raw, created 365 enrichment records, and loaded all 365 into weather_enriched. 
 
 The Prefect run showed all four tasks—extract, load_raw, transform, and load_enriched—as Completed, and none of the 
 tasks needed to retry. The LLM summaries in weather_enriched were generally useful because they provided a short 
 recommendation based on the weather conditions and the ML prediction. One summary that stood out was 
 "Given the mixed conditions with wind speed at 27.2 km/h and precipitation of 21.0 mm, it's not a good day for 
 running", because the strong wind and the substantial amount of precipitation can make it uncomfortable for running.
 
 If I deployed this pipeline to run daily, I would change the extraction step to dynamically fetch the previous day's weather data 
 and schedule the Prefect flow to run automatically each morning, while keeping the incremental check so 
 already-enriched dates are not processed again.